  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: We have only one completed experiment (config_001: RNA-only, single-profile, PCA-2000) yielding ~48.5% accuracy, which is a weak baseline. The most critical uncertainty for a multimodal cellular profiling study is whether the image modality carries independent predictive signal at all. Question being tested: config_010 (image-only, single-profile, ResNet-50) isolates the image modality's contribution while holding profile setting constant, giving a clean single-modality comparison against the RNA-only baseline. Why this is the best next experiment: (1) It addresses the highest-impact design decision—whether image features add value—before investing budget in the many multimodal fusion configurations. (2) If image-only performs comparably or better than RNA-only, it strongly motivates multimodal experiments; if it is much weaker, it signals that image encoders need improvement (e.g., ViT) or that RNA is the dominant signal. (3) Using ResNet-50 (a standard, well-calibrated encoder) keeps the test interpretable. (4) It is the minimal, single-variable change from the baseline, maximizing the information gained per experiment under a tight budget."
}

